 The list of discovered PuppetDB targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.puppetdbSDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
 
+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration allows retrieving scrape targets from [Scaleway Instances API](https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/instance/#path-instances-list-all-instances).
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # zone is an optional Scaleway zone to query instances from.
+    # By default, fr-par-1 is used.
+    #
+  - zone: "fr-par-1"
+
+    # project is an optional Scaleway project ID to filter discovered instances by.
+    #
+    # project: ...
+
+    # organization is an optional Scaleway organization ID to filter discovered instances by.
+    #
+    # organization: ...
+
+    # server is an optional Scaleway API server to query.
+    # By default, https://api.scaleway.com is used.
+    #
+    # server: "https://api.scaleway.com"
+
+    # port is an optional port to scrape metrics from. By default, port 80 is used.
+    #
+    # port: ...
+
+    # Scaleway authenticates API requests via a secret key passed in the `X-Auth-Token` header.
+    # It can be supplied via the `headers` HTTP API client option below.
+    headers: ["X-Auth-Token: <secret_key>"]
+
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+```
+
+Each discovered target has an [`__address__`](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/#how-to-modify-scrape-urls-in-targets) label set
+to `<public_ip>:<port>` if the instance has a public IP address, or to `<private_ip>:<port>` otherwise.
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during [relabeling](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/):
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the ID of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_hostname`: the hostname of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_type`: the commercial type of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_status`: the state of the instance (e.g. `running`, `stopped`).
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_zone`: the zone of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_organization_id`: the organization ID owning the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_project_id`: the project ID owning the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_private_ipv4`: the private IPv4 address of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv4`: the public IPv4 address of the instance, if any.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_tags`: comma separated list of tags assigned to the instance.
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
